		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "9d975f0c-a7cc-4367-8bfe-8d9c13b48932")
		(at 116.61 99.06 -90)
		(descr "Through hole straight socket strip, 2x10, 2.54mm pitch, double cols (from Kicad 4.0.7), script generated -- unmodified clone of the system Connector_PinSocket_2.54mm part, kept in the project library per convention. Used for J1 (TO_PANEL): the adapter plugs directly into the real front panel board's male header with no ribbon cable, so J1 needs a female socket. No pad renumbering needed here (unlike J1's old PinHeader-based part) -- verified empirically that placing this stock footprint's own native pad 1 at the real-world position 2.54mm further in local +Y than the old header-based part's origin reproduces every one of the 20 verified-correct pad positions exactly. See RC2014-I2C project NOTES.md.")
